Do not allocate the MTP drafter's embed_tokens and lm_head: vLLM throws them away.

For MTP drafters the proposer (v1/spec_decode/llm_base_proposer.py,
_maybe_share_embeddings and _maybe_share_lm_head) ALWAYS deletes the drafter's own
embed_tokens and lm_head after loading and points the drafter at the target
model's. Until that moment both copies are resident. Qwen3.5/3.6/3.8 have a
248,320-row vocabulary, so that is 2 x 2.37 GiB (bf16) allocated, loaded from the
checkpoint, and then freed.

On a 24 GiB card the second allocation does not fit next to a ~18 GiB model:
  torch.OutOfMemoryError: Tried to allocate 2.37 GiB ... 1.85 GiB is free
Measured identically on vLLM 0.22.1 and 0.28.0 with Qwen3.8-27B-MTP-NVFP4
(2026-09-19 / 2026-09-21), and on 2026-07-02 with Qwen3.6-27B-MTP-pi-tune-NVFP4.
It fails at MODEL LOAD, before any KV cache exists, so no serving flag
(--gpu-memory-utilization, --max-model-len, --enforce-eager) can reach it.

With this patch the drafter builds placeholders instead, skips those tensors in
load_weights, and the proposer's sharing step fills them in as before. Verified
2026-09-21 on RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell: "Model loading took 18.65 GiB" (17.86 GiB
body + the MTP layer), both "Sharing target model ..." lines logged, 40/40
requests served, 61.6 tok/s against 33.3 tok/s without MTP, mean acceptance
length 2.6-3.4 at 3 draft tokens.

Sharing only happens at pipeline-parallel size 1; the stock behaviour is kept
otherwise. DEVAI_MTP_SHARE_VOCAB_AT_INIT=0 restores it unconditionally.

Applies AFTER the HyperQwen series (qwen3_5-embed-quant and
qwen3_5-mtp-draft-vocab touch the same file). Validated against vLLM 0.28.0.

